#
# Fail-witness for the axis-is-not-the-dimension ban (ex:saAssessmentAxisNotAliasedToDimension):
# a fixture that declares gmeow:assessmentAxis a SUB-PROPERTY of gmeow:qualityDimension —
# exactly the aliasing the rubric must never carry. Under that triple an RDFS reasoner
# derives a gmeow:qualityDimension edge from every recorded axis, and a consumer would then
# be licensed to read the axis back off the dimension. It cannot: gmeow:axisDimension maps
# sixteen axes onto twelve dimensions, so three axes apiece collapse onto
# gmeow:qualityDimensionCompleteness and gmeow:qualityDimensionProjection, and two apiece onto
# gmeow:qualityDimensionDocumentation and gmeow:qualityDimensionProvenanceHonesty. The alias
# would silently merge those grades, and a per-axis ratchet reading the merged result would
# gate on an axis it never measured.
#
# Unioned with the rubric module by the gmeow:saFailWitness teeth check, this makes the
# mustNot ASK HOLD, proving the ban catches a real aliasing rather than passing vacuously.
# The real module must never carry this triple.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

gmeow:assessmentAxis rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:qualityDimension .
